  "conclusions": [
    "The zero-model organization workload is implemented and measured on JSON and SQLite. It uses actual bound actors, persistent deterministic decisions, temporal organization relations, commitments and conserved inventory.",
    "Both backends completed 30 simulated days for four employees, two managers and two departments: 120 fulfilled commitments, 360 decisions and 60 manager handoffs; all 120 deliveries retained the original debtor.",
    "JSON at a 60-second work budget stopped at day 24 with 97 accepted requests, 96 fulfilled and one pending. With a 120-second work budget it completed the same 30-day target. Both retained exact cold-recovery projections.",
    "The 500-employee/50-manager/20-department target initialized and reached 20 residents on both backends, but 30-second work budgets accepted only 37 SQLite and 22 JSON requests and did not advance to day one. All open commitments survived same-process and fresh-process recovery. The 15,000-request/30-day target is not verified."
  ],
  "limitations": [
    "This layer makes no model calls and sends no Team messages; it does not establish model throughput, provider token cost, model-context compaction or message capacity.",
    "The frozen deterministic work order is bounded, while full journal and Session history remain retained; disk-byte measurements are not retention guarantees.",
    "Observed long-history costs and population setup require further performance work or larger measured time budgets before claiming scenario C capacity. No deployment SLO or full-population 30-day completion is established."
  ]
}
